  "body": "This change depends on #3353. The PR now targets `main` so that deleting the parent branch will keep this review open. Integration commit `03929655b` joins the shared pass-start change with current main. Main includes #3113, which protects the move between Circular rings. The [Circular-only comparison](https://github.com/qsmits/Camcraft/compare/03929655b86b9a7b8e3dab176063a10fa621747b...c9b1ed4a65325c5dcaedc9369f4d9e55264c029b) starts at that integration commit.\n\nCircular now accepts Auto, Inside, and Outside in its Passes tab and through MCP. A saved project omits Auto. Inside cuts the smallest ring first. Outside cuts the largest ring first. Auto keeps the existing order, curved-floor depth sequence and CL output.\n\nFor a flat 10 mm radius pocket, a 6 mm cutter and a 2 mm stepover, the tool-center radii are 1, 3, 5 and 7 mm. Inside visits them in that order. Outside visits 7, 5, 3 and 1 mm. The tool completes the selected depth levels and lifts vertically to clearance before it crosses to the next ring.\n\nOn a curved floor, forced passes start their depth steps at stock height. The tool stays inside the current ring during entry. The checks cover the full helical orbit and its rounded endpoints. A short entry that cannot produce a valid arc uses the existing named fallback. The phase check uses the actual orbit on the outer ring when Inside approaches the rim.\n\n## Screenshots\n\n**Circular Passes before** (`03929655b`)\n\n![Circular Passes before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/87f3dd348a4dd3b9c5aaa0a21a741c51c2736d75/3441/3441-circular-before.png)\n\n**Circular Passes after** (`c9b1ed4a6`)\n\n![Circular Passes after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/87f3dd348a4dd3b9c5aaa0a21a741c51c2736d75/3441/3441-circular-after.png)\n\n**2D Offset Passes after** (`c9b1ed4a6`)\n\n![2D Offset Passes after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/87f3dd348a4dd3b9c5aaa0a21a741c51c2736d75/3441/3441-offset-after.png)\n\n## Verification\n\n- `mcp_circular_pass_start_is_an_undoable_project_setting` failed on test commit `5eba7638c` when MCP refused the valid setting as an unknown Circular field. The same test passed on the fix. It checks editing, undo, redo and saved projects. The Passes tab test selected both forced orders in the actual UI.\n- `circular_flat_pass_start_controls_every_ring_for_each_entry` passed in all nine combinations of pass order and entry type. An intermediate fix refused the final Inside helix. The corrected selector found a clear phase. The app verifier and post passed for the requested Inside paths.\n- The curved-floor tests check the first stock depth, all ring depths, higher stock and carried material, the full helical sweep, and the minimum postable chord. A low unused retract is permitted. The short-flute case held the post. Both existing Auto CL files matched byte for byte.\n- On `c9b1ed4a6`, the touched app binaries passed 379 tests. Motion passed 607 with 10 ignored. The restricted UI run passed 1,421 tests. All 11 tests that needed local graphics or loopback passed with local access. This gives 1,432 distinct UI passes and seven ignored. Strict Clippy passed for all app, motion, and UI targets.\n- The broad quick plan was a dry run. The focused app, motion and UI suites and strict Clippy ran on this head. Against integration base `03929655b`, all 245 selected release-mode execution steps completed. They recorded 107 passing ignored tests and 4 registered expected failures. Of the selected steps, 207 had no ignored cases to run. Each selected suite compiled on demand. The separate aggregate compile-only step was omitted.\n\nThe release gate also ran on trial merge `cdabd7105` of upstream `main` at `6e641dac7` and the reviewed head `c9b1ed4a6`. All 246 selected execution steps completed. 110 tests passed. The gate reproduced the four registered expected failures. It reported zero unexpected failures. 207 execution steps had no matching test to run. Each selected suite compiled on demand. This run omitted the separate aggregate compile-only step.\n\nNo physical machine run was performed.\n\nChangelog: Circular can cut rings from the inside or the outside. Auto keeps its existing path.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3359\n",
